  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday through Friday)\nIssued at 1257 AM CDT Sat Sep 19 2026\n\nBy Sunday and Monday, a couple of embedded disturbances aloft \nwill cruise through the region. This will act to weaken the ridge\nand allow for a medium chance (30-50%) for rain. An isolated\nstrong to severe thunderstorm cannot be completely ruled out \nacross the northern Big Country on Sunday afternoon and evening. \nThe main hazards would be large hail (1\" diameter) and damaging \nwinds (60-70 MPH). Otherwise, a weak cold frontal boundary may be \njust strong enough to drop temperatures a few degrees early next \nweek. By Tuesday, we may see highs in the upper 80s to lower 90s.",
